# npm install Restrictions

## Forbidden Flags

- **`--ignore-scripts`** — never use; postinstall/prepare scripts must run (Prisma generate, etc.)
- **`--legacy-peer-deps`** — never use; fix peer dependency conflicts properly instead

## Rationale

- Skipping scripts breaks Prisma Client generation, setup tasks, and other critical postinstall hooks
- Legacy peer deps hide real compatibility issues that should be resolved via version alignment or overrides

## When Dependencies Fail

- Resolve peer conflicts by aligning versions or using `overrides` in root `package.json`
- Fix Prisma/engine issues by ensuring correct dependency order and explicit `@prisma/engines` if needed
